@*
    Inline FOUC-prevention script. Place it inside <head> in App.razor, BEFORE the ZenithUI
    stylesheet link:

        <head>
            ...
            <ZenThemeScript />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/ZenithUI/zenith.css" />
        </head>

    Why this has to be inline and synchronous
    -----------------------------------------
    The server cannot know the viewer's stored preference: localStorage is not sent with the
    request. So the first HTML the browser receives is always the light palette. Without this
    script, a dark-mode user sees a white flash on every navigation until the Blazor circuit
    connects and JavaScript gets a chance to run - which can be hundreds of milliseconds.

    A synchronous inline script in <head> runs before the browser paints anything, so the
    attribute is already in place for the very first frame. A module, a deferred script, or
    anything loaded over the network would run too late to help.

    The logic below must stay in lockstep with wwwroot/js/zen-theme.js (same storage key, same
    attribute, same 'system means no attribute' rule). It is intentionally duplicated rather
    than imported, because importing would reintroduce the network round-trip this exists to
    avoid.
*@

<script>
    (function () {
        try {
            var mode = localStorage.getItem('zen-theme');

            // 'system' (or anything unrecognised) leaves the attribute off, which hands control
            // to the prefers-color-scheme media query in the stylesheet. Setting the resolved
            // value here instead would freeze the page against later OS changes.
            if (mode === 'light' || mode === 'dark') {
                document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-zen-theme', mode);
            } else {
                document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-zen-theme');
            }
        } catch (e) {
            // Storage unavailable (private browsing, partitioned iframe). Fall through to the
            // media query; a wrong-but-reasonable palette beats a broken page.
        }
    })();
</script>
